    "proposed_isolated_extension": [
      "Use a new versioned grader-only provider and fresh exact grant; preserve network=none, no host binds/listeners and no daemon/network/mount changes.",
      "Assign each allowed origin a distinct container-private loopback address, bind a per-origin listener and encode an immutable origin identity plus port in OPEN; host maps that identity to frozen public IPv4 tuples. A possible alternative is one independently bounded exec relay per origin. Both require fresh CPU framing tests.",
      "Change only the new grader private hosts mappings/listener setup outside /testbed; do not change host /etc/hosts, resolv.conf, routes or firewall. DNS resolution occurs only in the ordinary host helper through existing resolver before freezing selected public IPs.",
      "Forward raw HTTP/TLS bytes; retain original URL, HTTP Host, TLS SNI, certificate validation and original Requests CA. No TLS termination, injected CA, proxy rewriting or fabricated replies.",
      "Do not forward localhost:7777. The official local server and intentionally refused local HTTPS remain untouched.",
      "Use one combined aggregate cap across every origin/relay in a container, including redirects, rather than multiplying the allowance per domain. Log accepted/denied tuples, bytes, session close and namespace/ownership evidence.",
      "Do not install Requests-specific httpbin dependencies or private timeout route into Sphinx. Only minimal low-port binding capability may be necessary; need a scoped CPU/container diagnostic, no host NET_ADMIN or host changes."
